1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,200
Shopping agents can suggest products.

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:11,800
Woven uses WebMCP to finish a multi-item mission: one request, seven site tools,
complete verified carts, and a human-only purchase boundary.

3
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:17,400
Here is the live, top-level Woven Trail Market storefront.

4
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:26,000
The browser discovers seven purpose-built tools: start or inspect a mission, compare and select carts,
apply an approved swap, refresh price and stock, and verify an existing receipt.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:33,400
When the agent calls start_mission, the same page the person sees
moves from idle to verified kits.

6
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:37,800
Tool calls and human review share one state.
There is no DOM guessing, and no separate agent-only result.

7
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:59,000
Our test mission is a rainy-weekend camping kit for two, under S$300,
in one car boot, pickup-ready today.

8
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:08,200
Woven has to satisfy quantity, weather, compatibility, volume, current stock,
budget, and one pickup location at the same time.

9
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:13,500
Woven verifies five complete candidates and shows the best two.

10
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:24,500
TrailHaus is 7 units across 5 required categories, 89 L packed, a 3,000 mm rainfly,
and an exact S$231 total from one pickup point.

11
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:28,400
These are checkout-quality facts, not search snippets.

12
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:36,000
The agent may rerank the kits, select one,
or apply only a merchant-approved compatible alternative. Then it stops.

13
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Identity, exact checkout terms, confirmation secrets, and purchase authorization
are deliberately absent from the WebMCP tool surface.

14
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:54,000
The person completes the simulated identity handoff, sees every item, quantity, merchant,
pickup point, total, and expiry, then confirms directly.

15
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:00,300
Only that click can produce the simulated Visa result.
Woven accepts no card credentials and cannot make a live charge.

16
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:16,500
Implementation is equally explicit.

17
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:24,500
The top-level document supplies modelContext; Woven registers seven tools with closed schemas,
read-only annotations where appropriate, and one AbortSignal that removes the tool surface on navigation.

18
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:31,700
Every call enters the same server router and deterministic verifier
used by the visible storefront.

19
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:42,500
Woven shows what people and agents can do together: the agent handles reversible preparation,
the server enforces commerce truth, and the person owns identity and purchase.

20
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:46,500
The live app, public source, and demo are ready for review.

21
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:51,900
Seeded inventory, simulated identity, simulated payment—no live charge.
